    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d678">

                <pb facs="0654" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg564"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/3196</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Archangel</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-11-02T17:00:00+03:31"><hi rendition="#italic">November 2,
                                1918, 5 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 9, 1.08
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>540. My 532, October 31, 7 p.m. Chaikovski states situation quieted and
                    dissatisfaction among the 1,300 Russian soldiers liquidated, <pb facs="0655"
                        n="565" xml:id="pg565"/> with changes in command to ensue and segregation of
                    troops. While speaking of matter as unimportant his manner belied his words.
                    Your 331, October 31, 3 p.m., just received and being deciphered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
